    "final_answer": "Upgraded `settlement_reconcile.py` from v1 to v2.\n\n**Changes**\n- Switched endpoint from `/v1/graphql` to `/v2/graphql`.\n- Replaced the single-response query with the v2 paginated `settlements(first, after)` query using `nodes` + `pageInfo`.\n- Continues while `pageInfo.hasNextPage` is true, including after short or empty pages.\n- Deduplicates by settlement `id`, keeping the last version received, so amended settlements are emitted once.\n- Retries `429` responses using `Retry-After`, resending an identical request body.\n- Restarts traversal from the beginning if a cursor/GraphQL error occurs mid-pagination.\n\n**Verification against `http://the VM's public address:19121`**\n- Fetched `1873` settlements across `19` pages, including a short page.\n- Output contained `1873` lines and `1873` unique IDs.\n- Observed a live `429` with `Retry-After: 1`; the retry succeeded.\n- Result matched the v1 data exactly.\n- Also ran local mock tests for pagination, empty/short pages, amended IDs, 429 retry identity, and cursor-error restart \u2014 all passed.",
